{
  "method": "Coordinate search in log space from the site's defaults, one parameter set per (model, GPU) shared by all its tensor-parallel degrees. Loss: mean over calibration scenarios of (mean over requests of ln(ttft_ts/ttft_ref)^2 + ln(tpot_ts/tpot_ref)^2) / 2. Step ratios 2, 1.5, 1.25, 1.1, 1.05, 1.02; at each ratio, per parameter in the order mbu, mfu, hostMsBase, hostMsPerSeq, commEff, commLatencyUs, try value * ratio^j for j = -3..3 within bounds, keep the best, repeat until a sweep gains less than 1e-6. Bounds (decided 2026-11-16 from the measured vLLM runs and BLIS's range, before the refit): mbu [0.4, 0.95]; mfu [0.2, 0.9]; commEff [0.05, 1]; commLatencyUs [0.5, 50]; hostMsBase [0.01, 50]; hostMsPerSeq [0.001, 5]. commEff and commLatencyUs are fitted only for a group with several tensor-parallel degrees. specCost and linkGbps are then fitted alone by the same search (bounds [0, 1] and [1, 2000]), with the timing parameters held. Each group also reports the loss profile of mbu and mfu (the loss with the parameter held at three values and the others refitted); a profile within 25 percent of the best loss marks a parameter the data does not identify (the profile's refits use step ratios 2, 1.25, 1.05 only).",
